# Binary files must never go through EOL conversion. Without this file,
# core.autocrlf=true (a common system-level default on Windows) classifies
# small PDFs as text and rewrites their line endings at checkout — in
# pdfnative the golden page-tree fixtures grew by 305-616 bytes each while
# `git status` stayed clean, which is how the corruption went unnoticed. The
# blobs in git were always intact; only the working copy was damaged.
#
# Text files are LF in the repository AND in every working copy (eol=lf), so
# a Windows checkout produces the same bytes as CI and the sample baseline
# (tests/regression/baselines/samples.sha256.json) does not depend on the OS.
# The two blobs committed as CRLF before this line (both workflow files) were
# replaced by the 1.3.0 hardening commit; `verify:docs` (rule eol-lf) fails
# on any new one.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pdf   binary
*.icc   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary

# Generated files: collapsed in GitHub diffs and excluded from language stats.
.claude/rules/*.md                                  linguist-generated=true
tests/regression/baselines/samples.sha256.json      linguist-generated=true -diff
tests/__snapshots__/*.snap                          linguist-generated=true
package-lock.json                                   linguist-generated=true
